{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"The data in Table 8.2 are the result of a random survey of 39 national flags (with replacement between picks) from various countries. Let X = the number of colors on a national flag. <image> Construct a 95% confidence interval for the true mean number of colors on national flags. The 95% confidence interval is_____.\n\n(A) (2.92, 3.60)\n(B) (2.93, 3.60)\n(C) (2.92, 3.59)\n(D) (2.93, 3.59)\n\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly.","role":"user"}]}